WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.400
Titus, Chapter One.

2
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:17.333
Paul, a servant of God, and an apostle of Jesus Christ, according to the faith of God's elect, and the acknowledging of the truth which is after godliness; In hope of eternal life, which God, that cannot lie, promised before the world began;

3
00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:33.600
But hath in due times manifested his word through preaching, which is committed unto me according to the commandment of God our Saviour; To Titus, mine own son after the common faith: Grace, mercy, and peace, from God the Father and the Lord Jesus Christ our Saviour.

4
00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:48.933
For this cause left I thee in Crete, that thou shouldest set in order the things that are wanting, and ordain elders in every city, as I had appointed thee: If any be blameless, the husband of one wife, having faithful children not accused of riot or unruly.

5
00:00:48.933 --> 00:01:07.467
For a bishop must be blameless, as the steward of God; not selfwilled, not soon angry, not given to wine, no striker, not given to filthy lucre; But a lover of hospitality, a lover of good men, sober, just, holy, temperate; Holding fast the faithful word as he hath been taught,

6
00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:12.533
that he may be able by sound doctrine both to exhort and to convince the gainsayers.

7
00:01:12.533 --> 00:01:25.333
For there are many unruly and vain talkers and deceivers, specially they of the circumcision: Whose mouths must be stopped, who subvert whole houses, teaching things which they ought not, for filthy lucre's sake.

8
00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:32.133
One of themselves, even a prophet of their own, said, The Cretians are alway liars, evil beasts, slow bellies.

9
00:01:32.133 --> 00:01:33.600
This witness is true.

10
00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:42.800
Wherefore rebuke them sharply, that they may be sound in the faith; Not giving heed to Jewish fables, and commandments of men, that turn from the truth.

11
00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:52.533
Unto the pure all things are pure: but unto them that are defiled and unbelieving is nothing pure; but even their mind and conscience is defiled.

12
00:01:52.533 --> 00:02:00.533
They profess that they know God; but in works they deny him, being abominable, and disobedient, and unto every good work reprobate.

